bt_test.kr
# The --target=none provider tests need their programs INSIDE the repo:
# imports resolve relative to the importing file, so a program in /tmp would
# either fail to resolve "../std/uart_16550.kr" or silently pick up an
# installed stdlib instead of the tree under test. The directory is removed at
# the end of the block; this covers an aborted run.
/krc_pv_*/

# Built packages
packaging/deb/*.deb
packaging/deb/ext/

# Local-only working docs (planning/scope notes are not shipped)
/docs/MLRIFT_PORT_SCOPE.md

# Website (deployed separately)
/website/

# Internal docs
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/reviews/
/docs/PHASE_B_DESIGN.md

# Agent scratch tree (specs, plans, review reports). Only /docs/superpowers/
# was listed, so this 30 KB tree of working notes was UNTRACKED-BUT-VISIBLE and
# a single `git add -A` would have committed it. MLRift's .gitignore has
# carried this line for a while; this tree's did not.
.superpowers/

# --target=none acceptance-gate scratch (tests/target_none/prove_no_syscalls.sh)
/krc_tn_gate_*/
# ...and boot_gate.sh's sibling, which was missing. Both scripts mktemp their
# work dir INSIDE the repo on purpose (imports resolve against the importing
# file, so a /tmp dir would silently pick up an installed stdlib instead of the
# tree under test), so both leave a repo-root directory behind if the run is
# SIGKILLed past their traps. Only one of the two was listed.
/krc_boot_gate_*/

# Example build artifacts
examples/*/kernel.img
examples/*/*.ppm

# living-compiler backups written by `krc lc --fix`
*.lcbak
